  "message": "FICTIONAL PUBLIC DEMO — all people, addresses and events below are invented.\n\nI am Robin Senn. My spouse Sami Senn and I live together at Illustration Lane 8, apartment 4, Bern. This is our family home. A registered item delivered to me on 2 October 2026 contained the landlord's tenancy-termination notice, with a proposed end date of 31 March 2027. We dispute the termination and want the available evidence assessed.\n\nI attach our complete tenancy agreement and the original delivery record for the item addressed to me. The receipt proves what that delivery service recorded; it does not reproduce the notice or establish its legal validity. We do not have a scan of the notice yet. I cannot confirm whether Sami was served separately, and no separate spouse notice is supplied.\n\nWe report no rent arrears and no earlier complaint about tenancy rights. We have not decided whether to seek an extension; hardship and extension grounds remain unassessed. No challenge has been filed, no settlement reached and no response sent on our behalf.\n",
  "title": "Fictional intake · Robin and Sami’s family-home termination"
